Create ME table
What the model’s coefficients mean is explained in Longitudinal data and mixed models and Interactions; How this code does it describes what this table shows and doesn’t.


Click to show/hide R Code
# Mixed model of an outcome on visit (factor) by arm, with a random intercept
# for participant, returned as a flextable of the tidied coefficients. With
# an interaction variable, the model is visit by arm by that variable.
create_me_table &lt;- function(trial_data, outcome_of_interest,
                            interaction_variable = NULL) {
  # Primary analysis without interactions if interaction_variable is NULL
  if (is.null(interaction_variable)) {
    lmer(
      get(outcome_of_interest) ~ time_factor * studyarm +
        (1 | study_id_screening),
      data = trial_data
    ) %&gt;%
      tidy(., conf.int = TRUE) %&gt;%
      flextable() %&gt;%
      set_caption(paste0(outcome_of_interest, " vs. time")) %&gt;%
      return()
  } else {
    lmer_formula &lt;- paste0(
      outcome_of_interest, "~time_factor*studyarm*", interaction_variable,
      "+(1|study_id_screening)"
    ) %&gt;%
      as.formula()

    lmer(lmer_formula, data = trial_data) %&gt;%
      tidy(., conf.int = TRUE) %&gt;%
      flextable() %&gt;%
      set_caption(paste0(
        outcome_of_interest, " vs. time * ", interaction_variable
      )) %&gt;%
      return()
  }
}

Count models
Why the offset turns counts into rates, and why the exponentiated coefficients are incidence rate ratios, is in Longitudinal data and mixed models.


Click to show/hide R Code
# Negative binomial regression of each count on arm, with log follow-up time
# as an offset; incidence rate ratios, one row per outcome
count_model_table &lt;- NULL

for (outcome in count_outcomes) {
  outcome_formula &lt;- paste0(
    outcome, " ~ ", "studyarm + offset(log(followup_time_itt))"
  ) %&gt;%
    as.formula()

  outcome_table &lt;- glm.nb(outcome_formula, data = rescue_medication_merged) %&gt;%
    tbl_regression(
      exp = TRUE,
      show_single_row = "studyarm",
      label = list(studyarm ~ outcome)
    ) %&gt;%
    modify_header(update = list(label ~ "**Outcome**"))

  if (is.null(count_model_table)) {
    count_model_table &lt;- outcome_table
  } else {
    count_model_table &lt;- tbl_stack(list(count_model_table, outcome_table))
  }
}

Count interaction models
What each coefficient of an arm × subgroup model means is in Interactions, what the interaction p-value tests in What a p-value for interaction means, and how to get the IRR in each subgroup level in Effects behind an interaction.


